T8 additions include old/new host cache adapters, static graph orchestration,
quantized checkpoint materialization, failure cleanup, shared script cache,
four dialogue modes and immutable source-bound editor sessions. These
adaptations do not replace the original base revision recorded above.

The T8-owned native/kitchen_compat.py DLPack boundary interoperates with
Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen 0.2.40, source revision
f8b7e97a1418d2e529bd5405fbf86312be198ae6. It retains the installed host's
official Python attention function and CUDA extension; it does not bundle
or replace that implementation. The fixed-stride binding contract is in
comfy_kitchen/backends/cuda/dlpack_bindings.cpp in that source revision.
Host compatibility checks also use ComfyUI at
0b05cd8a3683cbf0c291b1472bb8b64da41de9ae; the bundled engine stays pinned
to the revision below.

